{%- comment -%}
  JOINTWELL v5 — the landing page.

  The design file this is built from kept markup, styles and behaviour in
  one document. Here the styles live in assets/jw-v5.css and the behaviour
  in assets/jw-v5.js, because large Liquid files have repeatedly failed to
  sync from GitHub on this store and the section this replaced was 132KB.
  What is left here is the markup and the only thing markup should own:
  the words, and where the numbers come from.

  EVERY PRICE ON THIS PAGE COMES FROM A SHOPIFY VARIANT. Nothing is typed
  in. Change a price in admin and the tiles, the CTAs, the sticky bar, the
  value stack and the checkout all move together, because they are all the
  same number. The one figure that is not a live price is the struck-out
  £65, which is the wrap's compare-at price, also from admin.

  THE ORDER IS A REAL FORM POST to /cart/add with return_to=/checkout, so
  it works with JavaScript broken, blocked or still loading. The script
  only keeps the hidden line items in step with the buttons.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    The wrap. The picker wins; the handles are the fallback so a rename in
    admin cannot strand the buy box. The list is in order of preference and
    every name this product has traded under is still in it, because each
    rename changed the handle and a single hardcoded one has stranded this
    buy box before. First one that resolves wins.
  endcomment
  assign wrap = section.settings.product
  if wrap == blank or wrap.id == blank
    assign wrap_handles = 'jointwell-heated-joint-massager,jointwell-heated-joint-wrap,thermora-heated-joint-massager,warmden-heated-knee-massager' | split: ','
    for h in wrap_handles
      assign candidate = all_products[h]
      if candidate != blank and candidate.id != blank
        assign wrap = candidate
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    Variants, by SKU first and position second. SKU is the better key in
    principle, but on this store every pack carries the same SKU, so
    position is what actually resolves them and the SKU pass is the thing
    that keeps working if that is ever fixed.
  endcomment
  for v in wrap.variants
    case v.sku
      when 'JW-WRAP-1'
        assign v_single = v
      when 'JW-WRAP-2'
        assign v_pair = v
      when 'JW-WRAP-4'
        assign v_four = v
    endcase
  endfor
  unless v_single
    assign v_single = wrap.variants[0]
  endunless
  unless v_pair
    assign v_pair = wrap.variants[1]
  endunless
  unless v_four
    assign v_four = wrap.variants[2]
  endunless

  comment
    THE FOUR-WRAP TILE. The product now carries a real four-pack variant, so
    the tile is that variant at quantity one and its price is whatever admin
    says — today £139, which is where the £34.75 a wrap below comes from.

    The fallback is kept because it is what made the tile honest before that
    variant existed: with no four-pack, the tile becomes the PAIR ordered
    TWICE at exactly two pairs' price, undiscounted. A tile advertising a
    saving the checkout will not honour is worse than one advertising none.
    Delete the four-pack variant in admin and this reverts on its own.
  endcomment
  assign four_qty = 1
  if v_four != blank and v_four.id != blank
    assign v_fourline = v_four
    assign four_c = v_four.price
  else
    assign v_fourline = v_pair
    assign four_qty = 2
    assign four_c = v_pair.price | times: 2
  endif

  comment
    The compression brace, the order bump. Resolved by handle rather than by
    a second picker: two "type": "product" settings in one schema is invalid
    Shopify syntax, and is what silently broke every GitHub sync of this file
    once before.

    Several handles, for the same reason the wrap has several. No product,
    no bump — the markup below checks before it draws anything.
  endcomment
  assign brace_handles = 'jointwell-compression-knee-brace,jointwell-compression-brace,compression-knee-brace' | split: ','
  for h in brace_handles
    assign candidate = all_products[h]
    if candidate != blank and candidate.id != blank
      assign brace = candidate
      break
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Prices, in cents, straight off the variants. _p suffixed values are the
    same figures in pounds, for the script, which animates numbers rather
    than strings and so cannot take a formatted price.
  endcomment
  assign single_c = v_single.price
  assign pair_c = v_pair.price
  assign was_c = v_single.compare_at_price
  if was_c == blank or was_c <= single_c
    assign was_c = single_c
  endif

  assign single_p = single_c | divided_by: 100.0
  assign pair_p = pair_c | divided_by: 100.0
  assign four_p = four_c | divided_by: 100.0

  comment
    Per-wrap figures. These are the bundles' real argument, and they are
    divided here rather than typed so a price change cannot leave the page
    claiming a discount that is no longer on offer.
  endcomment
  assign pair_each = pair_c | divided_by: 2 | money_without_trailing_zeros
  assign four_each = four_c | divided_by: 4 | money_without_trailing_zeros

  comment
    The brace. One and Two are separate variants with their own prices, so
    the bump never relies on a discount to make its own maths true.

    Which is which comes off the pack option, and the word a shop picks for
    "two" varies, so match a small set rather than one exact string. A brace
    built with no pack option at all comes out as all singles, the quantity
    row does not render, and the bump still works.

    The same pass builds the size-and-pack to variant-id map the script uses,
    so the two can never classify the same variant differently.
  endcomment
  assign two_words = 'Two,2,Pair,Twin,Two pack,2 pack,Two braces' | split: ','
  assign brace_n = 0
  capture brace_map
    for v in brace.variants
      assign is_two = false
      for w in two_words
        if v.option2 == w
          assign is_two = true
          break
        endif
      endfor
      assign pack = 1
      if is_two
        assign pack = 2
        unless brace_two
          assign brace_two = v
        endunless
      else
        unless brace_one
          assign brace_one = v
        endunless
      endif
      if brace_n > 0
        echo ','
      endif
      assign brace_n = brace_n | plus: 1
      assign bkey = v.option1 | append: '|' | append: pack
      echo bkey | json
      echo ': "'
      echo v.id
      echo '"'
    endfor
  endcapture
  assign brace_one_c = brace_one.price | default: 1900
  assign brace_two_c = brace_two.price | default: 2900
  assign brace_one_p = brace_one_c | divided_by: 100.0
  assign brace_two_p = brace_two_c | divided_by: 100.0
  assign brace_two_each = brace_two_c | divided_by: 2 | money_without_trailing_zeros

  comment
    The value stack. The wrap line is the compare-at price, so it is a
    figure the shop has actually charged. The three free lines are what
    those parts cost to buy separately; they are settings because only the
    buyer of the parts knows them.
  endcomment
  assign strap_c = section.settings.value_strap | default: 900
  assign cable_c = section.settings.value_cable | default: 600
  assign card_c = section.settings.value_card | default: 300
  assign box_c = was_c | plus: strap_c | plus: cable_c | plus: card_c
  assign box_p = box_c | divided_by: 100.0

  comment
    Temperature. Every figure on the page renders from these three, so a
    measurement can be corrected in one place instead of eleven.

    READ BEFORE CHANGING: the top figure has never been confirmed on a
    physical unit. It comes from the supplier pack. The safety copy leans on
    it, and so does the whole cordless-vs-corded argument. Measure it with
    an IR thermometer and set the real number here.
  endcomment
  assign t_min = section.settings.temp_min | default: 45
  assign t_max = section.settings.temp_max | default: 65
  assign t_low = section.settings.temp_typical | default: '45 to 50'

  comment
    Support. No number is invented: with the field empty the header and the
    footer fall back to the email address rather than printing a placeholder
    that rings a stranger.
  endcomment
  assign phone = section.settings.support_phone
  assign email = section.settings.support_email | default: 'support@velagoods.co.uk'

  comment
    A buy box that cannot resolve a variant is worse than no buy box: with
    JavaScript off it posts an empty line id and Shopify answers with its
    own error page. Decide once here, and let the form say so instead.
  endcomment
  assign wired = false
  if v_single != blank and v_single.id != blank
    assign wired = true
  endif

  comment
    Where a hash link has to go when this section is not the homepage.
  endcomment
  assign home = routes.root_url
  if template.name == 'index'
    assign home = ''
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The sizes offered are whatever the brace product actually has, so a size
  that sells out and is deleted in admin stops being offered here without
  anyone editing this file. The cm ranges are stated below, where the
  buttons are drawn.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- for opt in brace.options_with_values -%}
  {%- assign optname = opt.name | downcase -%}
  {%- if optname == 'size' -%}{%- assign brace_sizes = opt.values -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{% render 'jw-header', phone: phone, email: email, home: home %}

{%- comment -%}
  Everything assets/jw-v5.js needs from this store, in one object. The
  script states no price, no variant id and no image path of its own, so
  this is the only place the two can disagree — and they cannot, because
  the markup below is painted from the same variables.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  window.JW = {
    env: {% if section.settings.mock_mode %}'mock'{% else %}'live'{% endif %},
    phone: {{ phone | json }},
    email: {{ email | json }},
    companyNumber: {{ section.settings.company_number | json }},
    prices: {
      single: {{ single_p }},
      pair: {{ pair_p }},
      four: {{ four_p }},
      braceOne: {{ brace_one_p }},
      braceTwo: {{ brace_two_p }},
      box: {{ box_p }},
      braceValue: {
        "1": {{ section.settings.value_brace_one | default: 2500 | divided_by: 100.0 }},
        "2": {{ section.settings.value_brace_two | default: 5000 | divided_by: 100.0 }}
      },
      {%- comment -%}
        Quoted, because the form carries them as strings and because an
        unresolved variant must come out falsy. A bare 0 would do; "0" would
        not, and that is exactly the guard the script leans on.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      variants: {
        single: "{{ v_single.id }}",
        pair: "{{ v_pair.id }}",
        four: "{{ v_fourline.id }}",
        fourQty: {{ four_qty }}
      }
    },
    {%- comment -%}
      Built in the same pass that decided which variant is one brace and
      which is two, so the two cannot disagree. Keys are json-quoted rather
      than hand-escaped, because the script builds the same key from the
      data-size attribute, which the DOM hands back decoded: escaping one
      side and not the other is how a size with punctuation in it would
      silently stop resolving.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    braceVariants: { {{ brace_map }} },
    photos: {
      "kettle":          { s: "{{ 'jw-photo-kettle.jpg'          | asset_img_url: '500x' }}", s2: "{{ 'jw-photo-kettle.jpg'          | asset_img_url: '1000x' }}" },
      "armchair":        { s: "{{ 'jw-photo-armchair.jpg'        | asset_img_url: '500x' }}", s2: "{{ 'jw-photo-armchair.jpg'        | asset_img_url: '1000x' }}" },
      "crossword-elbow": { s: "{{ 'jw-photo-crossword-elbow.jpg' | asset_img_url: '500x' }}", s2: "{{ 'jw-photo-crossword-elbow.jpg' | asset_img_url: '1000x' }}" },
      "floor":           { s: "{{ 'jw-photo-floor.jpg'           | asset_img_url: '500x' }}", s2: "{{ 'jw-photo-floor.jpg'           | asset_img_url: '1000x' }}" },
      "garden-window":   { s: "{{ 'jw-photo-garden-window.jpg'   | asset_img_url: '500x' }}", s2: "{{ 'jw-photo-garden-window.jpg'   | asset_img_url: '1000x' }}" },
      "breakfast":       { s: "{{ 'jw-photo-breakfast.jpg'       | asset_img_url: '500x' }}", s2: "{{ 'jw-photo-breakfast.jpg'       | asset_img_url: '1000x' }}" }
    },
    reviews: [
      {%- comment -%}
        forloop.last is no use here: the last block may be an app block, and
        a dangling comma in an array literal leaves a hole rather than an
        error, which is the worst of both. Count the reviews instead.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign rn = 0 -%}
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- if block.type == 'review' -%}
          {%- if rn > 0 %},{% endif -%}
          {%- assign rn = rn | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- assign f = block.settings.photo_file -%}
          {%- if block.settings.photo != blank -%}
            {%- assign r1 = block.settings.photo | image_url: width: 62 -%}
            {%- assign r2 = block.settings.photo | image_url: width: 124 -%}
            {%- assign r3 = block.settings.photo | image_url: width: 186 -%}
          {%- elsif f != blank -%}
            {%- assign r1 = f | asset_img_url: '62x' -%}
            {%- assign r2 = f | asset_img_url: '124x' -%}
            {%- assign r3 = f | asset_img_url: '186x' -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign r1 = '' -%}{%- assign r2 = '' -%}{%- assign r3 = '' -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          { img: { s: {{ r1 | json }}, s2: {{ r2 | json }}, s3: {{ r3 | json }} },
            q: {{ block.settings.short | json }},
            n: {{ block.settings.carousel_name | default: block.settings.name | json }},
            s: {{ block.settings.stars | default: 5 }} }
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  };
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  A <div>, not a <main>: layout/theme.liquid already opened one around
  content_for_layout, and two of them is invalid HTML and two landmarks for
  a screen reader. The id and the skip-link target are unchanged.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div id="main" tabindex="-1">

{%- comment -%} ================= HERO ================= {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      {%- comment -%} Structure: STOP [resignation] / [three named symptoms] / [mechanism] / [outcome on the button]
           Alternatives, swap wholesale:
           B  STOP MANAGING IT   | For the Stiffness at Six, the Bannister You Now Hold, and the Chair You Plan Before You Sit   | Get your mornings back
           C  STOP SETTLING      | For Warmth That Fades, Creams That Do Nothing, and a Waiting List Measured in Years           | Try the one that holds
           D  STOP ACCEPTING     | That This Is Just What Sixty-Five Feels Like                                                   | Take back your stairs {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="kicker-shout">STOP SETTLING</span>
      <h1>For Joint Pain, Stiffness, and Letting One Knee Run Your Day</h1>

      <p class="sub"><strong>Knee, shoulder or elbow.</strong> The warmth everyone tells you helps, held at the temperature you set for a full thirty minutes. A wheat bag comes out scalding and it&#8217;s a cold lump by minute ten.</p>

      <div class="cta-unit">
        <a class="btn" href="#offer">Take your day back<small><span data-price>{{ single_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>, 90-day trial, free UK delivery</small></a>
        <div class="cta-bullets">
          <span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</i>90 days to try it, and we pay the return postage</span>
          <span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</i>2-year UK warranty</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="proof" data-proof>
        <div class="faces">
          <img src="{{ 'jw-review-sarah.jpg' | asset_img_url: '38x' }}" srcset="{{ 'jw-review-sarah.jpg' | asset_img_url: '38x' }} 1x, {{ 'jw-review-sarah.jpg' | asset_img_url: '76x' }} 2x, {{ 'jw-review-sarah.jpg' | asset_img_url: '114x' }} 3x" alt="" width="38" height="38" decoding="async">
          <img src="{{ 'jw-review-margaret.jpg' | asset_img_url: '38x' }}" srcset="{{ 'jw-review-margaret.jpg' | asset_img_url: '38x' }} 1x, {{ 'jw-review-margaret.jpg' | asset_img_url: '76x' }} 2x, {{ 'jw-review-margaret.jpg' | asset_img_url: '114x' }} 3x" alt="" width="38" height="38" decoding="async">
          <img src="{{ 'jw-review-linda.jpg' | asset_img_url: '38x' }}" srcset="{{ 'jw-review-linda.jpg' | asset_img_url: '38x' }} 1x, {{ 'jw-review-linda.jpg' | asset_img_url: '76x' }} 2x, {{ 'jw-review-linda.jpg' | asset_img_url: '114x' }} 3x" alt="" width="38" height="38" decoding="async">
          <img src="{{ 'jw-review-brenda.jpg' | asset_img_url: '38x' }}" srcset="{{ 'jw-review-brenda.jpg' | asset_img_url: '38x' }} 1x, {{ 'jw-review-brenda.jpg' | asset_img_url: '76x' }} 2x, {{ 'jw-review-brenda.jpg' | asset_img_url: '114x' }} 3x" alt="" width="38" height="38" decoding="async">
        </div>
        <span><b>{{ section.settings.customers }}</b> UK customers</span>
        <span class="stars" role="img" aria-label="Average rating {{ section.settings.rating }} out of 5">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span>
        <span><b>{{ section.settings.rating }}</b> from <b>{{ section.settings.review_count }}</b> reviews</span>
      </div>

      <div class="rcar" id="rcar" role="group" aria-label="What customers say">
        {%- comment -%} Slide one is in the markup so this is never an empty rectangle
             while the script loads, or if the script never arrives. The
             carousel adopts this node and appends the rest after it. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="rcar-win" id="rcar-win">
          {%- comment -%}
            Slide one is in the markup so this is never an empty rectangle
            while the script loads, or if the script never arrives. The
            carousel adopts this node and appends the rest after it, so it
            has to be the SAME review the script has at index 0 — hence the
            loop with a limit of one rather than a hand-typed copy.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'review' and first_rendered != true -%}
              {%- assign first_rendered = true -%}
              {%- assign f = block.settings.photo_file -%}
          <div class="rcar-slide on">
            {% if block.settings.photo != blank -%}
              <img src="{{ block.settings.photo | image_url: width: 62 }}" srcset="{{ block.settings.photo | image_url: width: 62 }} 1x, {{ block.settings.photo | image_url: width: 124 }} 2x, {{ block.settings.photo | image_url: width: 186 }} 3x" alt="" width="62" height="62" decoding="async">
            {%- else -%}
              <img src="{{ f | asset_img_url: '62x' }}" srcset="{{ f | asset_img_url: '62x' }} 1x, {{ f | asset_img_url: '124x' }} 2x, {{ f | asset_img_url: '186x' }} 3x" alt="" width="62" height="62" decoding="async">
            {%- endif %}
            <div>
              <p class="rcar-q">{{ block.settings.short }}</p>
              <div class="rcar-foot">
                <span class="rcar-who">{{ block.settings.carousel_name | default: block.settings.name }}</span>
                {% if block.settings.verified %}<span class="rcar-badge" role="img" aria-label="Verified buyer">&#10003;</span>{% endif %}
                <span class="stars" role="img" aria-label="Rated {{ block.settings.stars }} out of 5">{% for i in (1..block.settings.stars) %}&#9733;{% endfor %}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
        <div class="rcar-dots" id="rcar-dots"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-media">
      <img src="{{ 'jw-hero.jpg' | asset_img_url: '800x' }}"
           srcset="{{ 'jw-hero.jpg' | asset_img_url: '400x' }} 400w, {{ 'jw-hero.jpg' | asset_img_url: '600x' }} 600w, {{ 'jw-hero.jpg' | asset_img_url: '800x' }} 800w, {{ 'jw-hero.jpg' | asset_img_url: '1000x' }} 1000w, {{ 'jw-hero.jpg' | asset_img_url: '1200x' }} 1200w"
           sizes="(max-width:960px) calc(100vw - 44px), (max-width:1164px) 44vw, 484px"
           width="1024" height="1024" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
           alt="A woman in her sixties sitting at her kitchen table with the Jointwell wrap strapped over one knee, the controller resting on her lap and a cup of tea beside her.">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ================= THE NUMBERS =================
     No new claims: every figure here already appears elsewhere on the
     page. This world just says them at the volume it argues in. {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="band-warm" id="numbers">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="numbers">
      <div><span class="num">{{ section.settings.customers }}</span><span class="num-lab">UK customers</span></div>
      <div><span class="num">{{ section.settings.rating }}</span><span class="num-lab">from {{ section.settings.review_count }} reviews</span></div>
      <div><span class="num">90</span><span class="num-lab">days to decide</span></div>
      <div><span class="num">30</span><span class="num-lab">minutes, held</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ================= TRUST ================= {%- endcomment -%}
<section style="padding:0" data-mock>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="tp">
      <span class="stars" role="img" aria-label="Rated 5 out of 5">★★★★★</span>
      <span class="todo" data-mock>Trustpilot widget here — third-party proof outperforms on-page reviews for cold traffic</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ================= QUIZ ================= {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="band" id="quiz">
  <div class="wrap quiz">
    <h2 class="center">Which joint runs your day?</h2>
    <p class="center lede" style="margin-bottom:30px">Two questions and we'll show you how people with the same one use it. About ten seconds.</p>

    <noscript>
      <style>#quiz .q,#quiz .result{display:none}</style>
      <p class="center lede" style="margin:0 0 8px">This part needs JavaScript, which is switched off in your browser. <a href="#how">Read how it works</a> instead, or <a href="#offer">go straight to the offer</a>.</p>
    </noscript>

    <div class="q">
      <h3>1. The one you'd fix first</h3>
      <div class="opts" id="q1">
        <button class="opt" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-j="knee">A knee</button>
        <button class="opt" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-j="shoulder">A shoulder</button>
        <button class="opt" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-j="elbow">An elbow</button>
        <button class="opt" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-j="both">More than one</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="q q2" id="q2wrap">
      <h3>2. What have you already tried?</h3>
      <p class="hint">Tap all that apply. <span class="locknote" id="q2-lock">Answer the first question to unlock this.</span></p>
      <div class="opts" id="q2">
        <button class="opt" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-describedby="q2-lock" disabled>Hot water bottle or wheat bag</button>
        <button class="opt" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-describedby="q2-lock" disabled>Warming creams or gels</button>
        <button class="opt" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-describedby="q2-lock" disabled>Painkillers</button>
        <button class="opt" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-describedby="q2-lock" disabled>Physio</button>
        <button class="opt" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-describedby="q2-lock" disabled>Injections</button>
        <button class="opt" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-describedby="q2-lock" disabled>Nothing much yet</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="vh" id="result-status" role="status"></p>
    <div class="result" id="result" role="region" aria-label="Your result" tabindex="-1"></div>
    <p class="center"><a class="skip" href="#story">Skip this, take me to Paula's story</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ================= PAULA ================= {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="story" id="story">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <p class="kicker">Customer story. Paula, 65, in her own words.</p>
    <h2>I was going up the stairs on my hands and knees.</h2>

    {%- comment -%} v4 had no photograph of Paula anywhere in her own story {%- endcomment -%}
    <figure class="story-portrait" data-mock>
      <div class="ph" style="aspect-ratio:16/10"><span><b>Photo needed</b>Paula at the bottom of her stairs, hand on the bannister. Not smiling at camera. The story is evidence only if there's a face attached to it.</span></div>
      <figcaption>Paula at home in Wetherby. She ordered in March.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>Not every day. But often enough that I'd stopped being surprised by it. For a year before that I'd told myself it was just stiffness, you get to sixty-five and things creak, and then I noticed I'd started going up sideways, one foot at a time, and I couldn't remember deciding to do that.</p>

    <p>After the stairs it was the chair. You work out how you're getting up before you've even sat down. Then the car, and that pause before you put your weight on it, hoping nobody's watching. Then the garden, which got away from me completely. Then sleep.</p>

    <p class="pull">Nobody warns you how small your life gets while you're busy managing it.</p>

    <h3>What the GP could do, and what she couldn't</h3>

    <p>I went eventually. Everyone did their best. Eight minutes, wear and tear, very common, paracetamol and keep it moving. The physio letter took ten weeks. Six sessions and a sheet of exercises for the landing carpet, and by session four I'd stopped and neither of us mentioned it.</p>

    <p>The injection worked. Properly worked. For about ten weeks. Then one morning it was back, and they can only do that a few times a year, and had I thought about a replacement. Referred, not booked. Nobody says how long the list is. I looked it up and wished I hadn't.</p>

    <p>None of it is anyone's fault. The GP has eight minutes, the physio has six sessions, the surgeon has a list. It's just that nobody's job is to get you up the stairs <em>this month</em>.</p>

    <h3>What I tried while I waited</h3>
    <ul class="tried">
      <li><i class="cross" aria-hidden="true">✕</i><span><b>The wheat bag.</b> Helped for ten minutes. Then I was back at the microwave for the fourth time that night.</span></li>
      <li><i class="cross" aria-hidden="true">✕</i><span><b>The creams.</b> Warm on the skin, nothing in the joint, and it came off on my trousers.</span></li>
      <li><i class="cross" aria-hidden="true">✕</i><span><b>The physio.</b> Lovely woman. Six sessions, then a ten-week wait to be seen again.</span></li>
      <li><i class="cross" aria-hidden="true">✕</i><span><b>The paracetamol.</b> Takes the edge off. I didn't want to be on it every day for the rest of my life.</span></li>
    </ul>

    <p>None of it failed because my knee was too far gone. It failed because every single one of them gives you warmth that fades.</p>

    <p>I found this in a Facebook group for osteoarthritis. I was sceptical, I'd already tried the lot. Then I saw the ninety-day trial. If it doesn't work, send it back. So I thought, go on then. What is there to lose.</p>

    <div class="cta-unit" style="text-align:left">
      <a class="btn" href="#offer">Try it for 90 days<small><span data-price>{{ single_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>, free tracked UK delivery</small></a>
