            <div class="size-row" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="sql" id="sqty">
              <button class="size wide" type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="true" data-sp="{{ brace_one_p }}" data-pack="1">One, {{ brace_one_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}<small>&nbsp;</small></button>
              <button class="size wide" type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-sp="{{ brace_two_p }}" data-pack="2">Two, {{ brace_two_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}<small>{{ brace_two_each }} each, so one can be in the wash</small></button>
            </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            <p class="size-help">Measure round the middle of your knee with your leg straight. No tape measure? A length of string against a ruler does the same job. Between two sizes, take the larger one. If it's wrong when it arrives, the 90 days covers a swap and we pay the postage both ways.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <ul class="incl">
          <li><span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</i> The Jointwell wrap</span><span class="v">{{ was_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span></li>
          <li><span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</i> Shoulder and elbow extension strap</span><span class="v"><s>{{ strap_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s> <span class="free">Free</span></span></li>
          <li><span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</i> USB-C charging cable</span><span class="v"><s>{{ cable_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s> <span class="free">Free</span></span></li>
          <li><span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</i> Warm-up routine card, large print</span><span class="v"><s>{{ card_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s> <span class="free">Free</span></span></li>
          <li><span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</i> 2-year warranty and 90-day trial</span><span class="v free">Included</span></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="totals"><span>Total value<span id="val-n"></span></span><span id="val">{{ box_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span></div>
        <div class="totals pay"><span>You pay</span><span id="pay">{{ single_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span></div>

        <p class="compare">One physio session is about {{ section.settings.compare_physio | default: 5000 | money_without_trailing_zeros }}. One private injection is about {{ section.settings.compare_injection | default: 25000 | money_without_trailing_zeros }}. The waiting list is measured in years. This is <span data-price>{{ single_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>, once.</p>

        <button class="btn" type="submit" id="buy"{% unless wired %} disabled{% endunless %}><span class="buy-label">Try it for 90 days</span><small>You pay <span id="cta-p">{{ single_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span> today</small></button>
        <p class="field-msg{% unless wired %} is-error{% endunless %}" id="buy-note" role="alert"{% if wired %} hidden{% endif %}>{%- unless wired -%}We cannot take the order on the page just now. Email {{ email }} and we will take it by hand.{%- endunless -%}</p>
        <div class="cta-bullets" style="margin-top:12px">
          <span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</i>We pay the return postage</span>
          <span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</i>No reason needed</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pay-icons">{%- assign pays = section.settings.payment_names | default: 'Visa, Mastercard, Amex, PayPal, Apple Pay, Google Pay' | split: ',' -%}{%- for p in pays -%}<span>{{ p | strip }}</span>{%- endfor -%}</div>
        <p class="safety">A comfort device, not a medical treatment. If you have diabetes, circulation problems or reduced skin sensation, check with your GP before using heat.</p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ================= FAQ ================= {%- endcomment -%}
<section id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="center">Questions people ask before they buy</h2>
    <p class="center lede">Straight answers. If yours isn't here, ring us.</p>
    <div class="faq">
      <details open><summary>Isn't this just a heating pad with extra steps?</summary><div class="a"><p>A heating pad gives you heat that fades, or heat that ties you to a wall socket. Jointwell holds whichever level you pick for a full 30 minutes. It adds vibration massage at three strengths, straps on so it stays put, and runs cordless in any chair in the house.</p></div></details>

      {%- comment -%} moved to position 2: it's the objection sitting unanswered while she reads everything else {%- endcomment -%}
      <details><summary>When will it arrive?</summary><div class="a"><p>We ship in batches direct from the maker rather than holding stock in a UK warehouse, which is most of the reason this costs {{ single_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }} instead of {{ 8900 | money_without_trailing_zeros }}. The next batch goes out <span class="d-ship">Thursday</span> and most orders arrive within 7 to 10 working days, occasionally up to 14. Every order is tracked and we email you the link the moment it leaves us.</p><p>Your 90-day trial starts the day it arrives, not the day you order, so the wait doesn't eat into it. The morning routine, if you add it, is emailed within the hour.</p></div></details>

      <details><summary>Does the copper in the brace do anything?</summary><div class="a"><p>No, and we'd rather say so. Copper-threaded supports have been tested against identical ones without copper and they perform the same. Companies have been fined for claiming otherwise. It's a copper-coloured knit, and that's all it is.</p><p>What does do something is the compression. A snug knit holds the joint steady, keeps warmth in, and gives you a bit more sense of where the leg is when you're on uneven ground. That's worth {{ brace_one_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }} to a lot of people. The metal in the thread isn't.</p></div></details>

      <details><summary>Will it work for me? My joints have been like this a long time.</summary><div class="a"><p>It isn't a cure and we won't pretend otherwise. Nobody can promise what it'll do for your joint. What we can promise is warmth at the level you choose, held for thirty minutes, with massage alongside it. The 90-day trial is there so your own knee gets the deciding vote rather than our copy.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Will it fit me?</summary><div class="a"><p>One size, 46 cm across and 30 cm tall, with a 55 cm strap span. It fits either knee, and the extension strap in the box takes it round a shoulder or up an arm to the elbow. If it doesn't fit you, the 90-day trial covers a full refund and we pay the return postage.</p><figure class="rounded" style="margin-top:14px"><img src="{{ 'jw-dimensions.jpg' | asset_img_url: '740x' }}" srcset="{{ 'jw-dimensions.jpg' | asset_img_url: '380x' }} 380w, {{ 'jw-dimensions.jpg' | asset_img_url: '740x' }} 740w, {{ 'jw-dimensions.jpg' | asset_img_url: '1000x' }} 1000w" sizes="(max-width:784px) calc(100vw - 44px), 740px" width="1000" height="1000" alt="The wrap measures 46 cm across with a 55 cm strap span" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div></details>
      <details><summary>Is it safe? Will it burn me?</summary><div class="a"><p>Heat can burn skin if it's too hot, held too long, or used by someone who can't feel it properly. So: start at level 1 or 2, wear it over clothing rather than bare skin, and only go higher if it stays comfortable. Every session ends itself after 30 minutes, so it can't be left running, and you can stop it at any point.</p><p>Don't use it while asleep, over broken skin, or on a joint that's hot, red and swollen. If you have diabetes, circulation problems, reduced feeling in your skin, or you're under medical care for that joint, ask your GP before using any heat product. If the skin goes red and stays red after you take it off, that level is too high for you.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>How do I know this isn't another Facebook gadget?</summary><div class="a"><p>Fair question, because this market is full of them. There's a UK returns address, UK support on a landline, a 2-year warranty, and a 90-day trial where we pay the postage back. We're a registered UK company and the number is in the footer. The reviews on this page are from customers with an order on file, in their own words. Junk sellers can't afford the guarantee.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Can I use it after a knee replacement?</summary><div class="a"><p>Ask your surgeon or physio first, and follow what they say. Many people are told heat is fine once the wound has fully healed, but that's their call, not ours. If they say yes, most people use it as the warm half hour before their exercises.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>How do I charge it, and how long does a charge last?</summary><div class="a"><p>It charges over USB-C with the cable in the box, the same cable as most phones. It has a 3000 mAh battery, which most people find covers about four sessions. The panel shows the battery level.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Who shouldn't use it?</summary><div class="a"><p>Anyone who's been told to avoid heat on that joint. If you have diabetes, circulation problems, reduced feeling in your skin, a pacemaker, an unhealed wound or a joint that's hot, red and swollen, talk to your GP before using any heat product. Don't use it while asleep, over broken skin, or on a child. If you're pregnant or under medical care for the joint, ask first. It's a comfort device, not a treatment, and your GP's word beats ours.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What happens if I send it back?</summary><div class="a"><p>Email us within 90 days of delivery. We send you a UK returns address and a postage label. Post it back, and we refund what you paid in full once it arrives. You don't pay the postage and you don't have to give a reason, though we'd like to hear it.</p></div></details>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-unit">
      <a class="btn btn-auto" href="#offer">Try it for 90 days<small><span data-price>{{ single_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>, free tracked UK delivery</small></a>
      <div class="cta-bullets"><span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</i>We pay the return postage</span><span><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</i>2-year UK warranty</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ================= EMAIL: deliberately quieter than the buy button ================= {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="email-cap band">
  <div class="wrap narrow center">
    <h2>Not ready? Take the seven-morning routine instead.</h2>
    <p>Seven mornings, one page each, in large print you can read without your glasses. Kettle on, joint warm, then the day. Free, by email.</p>
    {%- comment -%}
      Shopify's own customer form. It posts natively, Shopify records the
      subscriber and redirects back here with ?customer_posted=true, and the
      confirmation below is rendered in Liquid rather than by the script.
      The routine itself is sent by whatever is listening to the
      "seven-morning-routine" tag in the email tool.

      assets/jw-v5.js only validates the address before the post, so a typo
      is caught here rather than on a round trip.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- form 'customer', id: 'email-form', novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
      <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter, seven-morning-routine">
      {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
        <p class="ef-done" role="status"><i class="tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</i><span>On its way to <b>{{ form.email }}</b>. Morning one lands within the hour &mdash; if it does not, have a look in the junk folder.</span></p>
      {%- else -%}
      <div class="ef">
        <label class="vh" for="email-input">Email address</label>
        <input id="email-input" name="contact[email]" type="email" placeholder="Email address"
               value="{{ form.email }}"
               autocomplete="email" inputmode="email" spellcheck="false" maxlength="254"
               required aria-describedby="email-help"{% if form.errors %} aria-invalid="true"{% endif %}>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost" type="submit" id="email-btn" style="width:auto;flex:none">Send it</button>
      </div>
      <p class="field-msg{% if form.errors %} is-error{% endif %}" id="email-msg" role="alert"{% unless form.errors %} hidden{% endunless %}>{%- if form.errors -%}{{ form.errors.messages['email'] | default: 'That address was not accepted. Check it and press Send it again.' }}{%- endif -%}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endform -%}
    <p id="email-help" style="font-size:var(--t-sm);margin-top:14px;color:var(--ink-2)">We send the PDF, then the occasional email. Unsubscribe with one click.</p>
  </div>
</section>

</div>

{%- comment -%}
  The sticky buy bar. It quotes the wrap-plus-brace total, so it is the one
  price on the page that can differ from the tier tiles, and deliberately:
  it is what she would pay if she pressed the button now.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="sticky" id="sticky">
  <div class="p"><span id="s-price">{{ single_c | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span><small>90 days, postage paid</small></div>
  <a class="btn" href="#offer">Try it for 90 days<small>Free UK delivery</small></a>
</div>

